WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:07.360
If you were confused at all about what exactly
happens the ending of Season 2, then stick

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.470
around to the end of this video.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:12.140
Sponsored by CryptTV.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:20.070
Welcome back to Things You Missed -- the year
is 1930, and not more than 11 seconds into

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:23.970
season 2, we've already got a guy going on
a rampage against his family.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:25.520
Why is this guy so angry?

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.930
And what does this all have to do with the
rest of the season, taking place on a rural

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:29.930
farmhouse?

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:31.880
What is the significance of this place: "Harbor"?

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.400
Why does Look-See come after this family,
and most importantly, what does any of this

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.360
have to do with any of Season 1?

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:40.400
These are all questions I'll be answering
on today's episode, but let's start at the

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.900
beginning of Season 2 Episode 1.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.050
Our location is New York City and this man,
Robert Capshaw, has just finished taking out

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.870
his family and I'm not talking about taking
them out for dinner.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:04.879
He hears the angry mob outside and finishes
the job by slitting his own throat.

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:08.910
The blood lands on this newspaper article
of Robert and his twin brother, James Capshaw.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:12.720
The spatter only covers Robert's half of the
photo, telling us that his brother is probably

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:13.720
still alive.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:17.140
This same trick using the blood to show who's
no longer alive is used again later in the

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.580
season on the daughter's drawing of the family.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.750
But why did Robert go crazy on his family?

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.630
The answer is in the setting.

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:26.970
As we saw earlier, this scene takes place
in March of 1930.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:30.909
It looks like the Capshaw Twins opened their
bank in the heat of the Great Economic Depression.

00:01:30.909 --> 00:01:35.360
For all you international viewers, not a good
time to open a bank in the USA.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.180
Now the other brother, James Capshaw, took
the dignified approach and got the heck out

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:42.520
of there, he moved his family to this remote
farmhouse.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.100
This is day to night transition is really
cool.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.080
Not only does it remind me of Hereditary...

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.811
but instead of using that annoying click noise
that the daughter in Hereditary makes, we

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:01.760
hear one tick from the stopwatch that Look-See
carries around.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:07.500
Using the stopwatch to show the passage of
time in Look-See?

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:08.510
Very cool.

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:12.220
I couldn't help but think that this next scene
was another homage to a 2018 horror movie.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:14.740
Was anyone else reminded of A Quiet Place?

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.810
So anyway, James Capshaw goes to check things
out at the barn, when he finds a foreclosure

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:41.360
notice from his own bank.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.620
Interesting note here, this stuff at the farmhouse
doesn't take place right after the scene in

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:45.620
New York City.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:48.060
The date of the foreclosure notice is Monday
August 1st.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.810
The next time August 1st falls on a Monday
after this opening scene, assuming that this

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:55.260
series uses real-world calendars, is August
1932.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:58.690
So two years go by between this and this.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:02.640
But it seems that even in these two years,
James hasn't let go of the fact that his business

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.080
failed, because as we've seen in previously
in Season 1...

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:15.780
The fact that James's note is written on a
dollar bill is further proof that it's the

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:19.810
bank started by him and his brother that he
was unable to release when he started this

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:21.060
new life in the country.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:24.330
We never actually get to see what body part
Look-See would have taken from him though,

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:28.319
because our buddy Dead Meat beats him to the
kill, marking probably the first time that

00:03:28.319 --> 00:03:30.740
James has added to his own Kill Count.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.459
Which I think might be cheating in a way.

00:03:32.459 --> 00:03:36.250
I don't know, I don't make the rules, but
if I went onto a horror movie set and placed

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:40.269
a bunch of Things You Missed around, would
that really be fair?

00:03:40.269 --> 00:03:44.780
To add to the mystery in a sense, one of the
thieves gets stabbed by a pitchfork off camera,

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:47.580
and we never see if Look-See is responsible
or not.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:51.280
I personally don't think he would have gotten
that deep of a stab just from falling on the

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:55.360
fork, but if Look-See is responsible, then
this is the only victim who doesn't receive

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.360
a note.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.590
Also, no body part is taken from this victim.

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:02.520
I think this is a new side of Look-See -- like
if you try to interfere with his dealings,

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:04.319
he'll just straight up kill you.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:05.640
Nightmare on Elm St. anyone?

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:10.590
Before we move on from this first episode,
I think it's important to note that each character's

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:12.850
fatal flaw is setup here in episode 1.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.940
The second episode is about the other thief.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.829
We can see his remorse start to kick in when
blood starts to shed, something he probably

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:21.359
did not sign up for when he agreed to become
a thief.

00:04:21.359 --> 00:04:25.009
He finds that his pocket watch has been replaced
by the Look-See watch at the end of episode

00:04:25.009 --> 00:04:28.689
1, and the second episode finds him regretting
his actions, having nightmares about his dead

00:04:28.689 --> 00:04:32.629
thief buddy (who by the way looks way too
happy to have a pitchfork going through his

00:04:32.629 --> 00:04:36.869
torso), and eventually Look-See rips him in
half, which is representative of him getting

00:04:36.869 --> 00:04:40.669
half of the share of whatever it was they
were stealing, with the third guy out of the

00:04:40.669 --> 00:04:41.669
picture.

00:04:41.669 --> 00:04:45.369
The wife, Mary Capshaw, can be seen clutching
her pearls in the first episode, which she

00:04:45.369 --> 00:04:47.930
does again in her episode, episode 3.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:51.720
You can just see her general discomfort being
at the farm house, and her episode's title,

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:55.839
The Second Love, tells me that her love for
her family falls second compared to material

00:04:55.839 --> 00:05:00.110
things like her fancy New York apartment,
her necklace and high heels.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:03.719
She's ultimately given the choice between
her family and her material possessions when

00:05:03.719 --> 00:05:07.990
her deceased son appears before her, with
her necklace that was broken in the previous

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.469
scene, now fully in tact.

00:05:09.469 --> 00:05:13.569
She goes for the necklace first, and as you
can probably imagine, Look-See doesn't like

00:05:13.569 --> 00:05:17.039
that, and takes her heart, because her heart
was in the wrong place.

00:05:17.039 --> 00:05:22.539
She was in that marriage out of love for money
and material things, not love for her family.

00:05:22.539 --> 00:05:25.999
Then we've got the older brother, David Capshaw,
played by my buddy Johnny Berchtold.

00:05:25.999 --> 00:05:29.830
He can be seen carrying around this bear,
which formerly belonged to his late little

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:30.830
brother.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:34.129
I know a lot of people were confused by his
fatal scene, because he eventually does rip

00:05:34.129 --> 00:05:37.460
the bear’s head off in an attempt to show
Look-See that he’s not holding onto his

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:40.879
deceased sibling, however, he still does pay
the price.

00:05:40.879 --> 00:05:45.039
I would compare this to the the woman letting
go of the ring in the very first episode in

00:05:45.039 --> 00:05:49.020
season 1 and, and the father from season 1
who throws away his dead daughter’s birthday

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:50.020
cake.

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:52.520
Despite the fact that these characters are
able to let go of their physical possessions,

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:56.580
they are still targeted, because what Look-See
is looking for is an emotional release, and

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:01.149
David Capshaw never actually has that moment,
so he’s left with his head turned around

00:06:01.149 --> 00:06:02.149
180°.

00:06:02.149 --> 00:06:05.449
Like the father from Season 1, he is punished
because he’s still looking backwards, not

00:06:05.449 --> 00:06:06.449
forwards.

00:06:06.449 --> 00:06:09.811
So that covers all of the characters who had
their lives taken by Look-See, but there are

00:06:09.811 --> 00:06:14.249
also two characters who survive this time
around: Dead Meat's character Raymond, and

00:06:14.249 --> 00:06:16.409
the little girl, Leah Capshaw.

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:19.940
Leah seems to be one who's working with Look-See
this season, leaving the note on the back

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:23.839
of her picture, crossing off the family members
as she takes them out and being the only one

00:06:23.839 --> 00:06:26.770
to see Look-See early on and not really look
scared.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:30.259
I think Leah already had an encounter with
Look-See and she was able to release whatever

00:06:30.259 --> 00:06:34.470
it was she was holding in, just like Jenni
was eventually able to do in Season 1, before

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:36.050
becoming Look-See's assistant.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:40.550
Leah also bears a strong resemblance to the
dead daughter in Season 1 Episode 3, more

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:41.610
on that later.

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:44.900
Then we've got Raymond, who gets his buddy's
blood poured on him.

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:45.600
Carrie anyone?

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:53.700
and Look-See curiously just lets him go.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:57.119
In order to explore the reason why, I’m
going to refer to James’s recent Kill Count

00:06:57.119 --> 00:06:58.360
video on Dead Meat.

00:06:58.360 --> 00:06:59.360
Roll it.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:03.259
"But a deeper look into Raymond's soul, murder
and all, leaves Look-See a little less smiley

00:07:03.259 --> 00:07:05.539
than usual, and he drops Raymond to the ground.

00:07:05.539 --> 00:07:09.330
Guess this guy didn't have anything to release,
so he takes all of his pieces and walks off

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:10.330
into the woods."

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:14.349
So my analysis of what's happening here is
that Raymond is a sociopath, he doesn't hold

00:07:14.349 --> 00:07:16.860
onto anything, so he has nothing to release.

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:20.009
I also think he's most likely going to be
working with Look-See in the future as one

00:07:20.009 --> 00:07:22.159
of the assistants, just like Jenni and Leah.

00:07:22.159 --> 00:07:25.990
I think the shot where Raymond is first introduced
also kind of suggests that there is some similarity

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:27.220
between him and Look-See.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:45.800
Also, at the very end of James's Kill Count
video, there's another little clue.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:49.659
"And of course, huge thanks to CryptTV for
partnering with me for this Kill-Count.

00:07:49.659 --> 00:07:52.610
Again make sure you subscribe to them, because
there will be more of me on that channel in

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:53.649
the future."

00:07:53.649 --> 00:07:56.089
Just saying, he's probably not making that
up.

00:07:56.089 --> 00:08:00.960
But now we can get into the real interesting
Things You Missed -- the clues about the ending.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:09.220
After a hand comes out of the teddy bear...

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:10.240
Evil Dead 2 anyone?

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:16.920
and Look-See ultimately kills David, the little
sister can finally scratch off the last of

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:20.369
her family members and she returns to Look-See
with the stop-watch.

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:21.980
Then... this happens.

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:44.720
Notice how the new hands are wearing blue
gloves instead of red.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:48.769
Also, notice if you look at the shadow, this
new Look-See has something attached to its

00:08:48.769 --> 00:08:49.769
head.

00:08:49.769 --> 00:08:52.090
Let's look back at the original drawing done
by Leah.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:55.570
You can see the Look-See hiding in the dark,
looming above the Capshaw family.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:59.800
You can see the Dad, the Mom, the brother,
the sister and the deceased younger brother

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:01.040
with his teddy bear.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.529
But what's this other character hiding in
the dark behind Look-See?

00:09:04.529 --> 00:09:06.649
I think that, is the second Look-See.

00:09:06.649 --> 00:09:10.140
If the original is made up of the body parts
of those who could not release and wears a

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:15.000
suit, maybe this other version, essentially
the baby Look-See, wears a bow on it's head.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:18.399
I think the new Look-See will be made up of
the the body parts acquired throughout Season

00:09:18.399 --> 00:09:19.399
2.

00:09:19.399 --> 00:09:22.389
You can even see that the head is divided
vertically, much like the thief who got torn

00:09:22.389 --> 00:09:23.389
in half.

00:09:23.389 --> 00:09:26.740
But what happens with this second Look-See
and how does that affect the original Look-See?

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:32.420
I think now is a good time to address the
timeline of events.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:36.500
Obviously both seasons take place in the past,
but where do they fall chronologically?

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:41.230
We know the exact date of Season 2, but we
don't know exactly when Season 1 takes place.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:45.240
The episode titles suggest that season 2 takes
place after, like how the first season has

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:49.040
an episode called The Wedding Hand and the
second season has an episode called The Second

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.040
Hands.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:53.269
Or how The Mistress Mind in the first season
has the counterpart, The Second Love in Season

00:09:53.269 --> 00:09:54.269
2.

00:09:54.269 --> 00:09:57.620
However, I've come to the conclusion that
Season 2, is a prequel.

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:01.170
In rewatching Season 1, I noticed this photo
with a pickup truck in the background.

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:06.319
It looks like a more modern vehicle, and I'm
no car expert, but I looked up what pickup

00:10:06.319 --> 00:10:10.069
trucks look like in the 30s and since then,
and came to the conclusion that Season 1 is

00:10:10.069 --> 00:10:11.930
more or less modern day.

00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:15.620
That's when it all came together for me about
how the two seasons, are related.

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:24.520
The end of Season 2 shows the creation of
the new Look-See, then pulls out and shows

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:27.880
us again, the name of the area they are in:
Harbor.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:32.080
In Episode 4 of Season 1 thirteen high school
kids are poisoned and die.

00:10:32.089 --> 00:10:35.470
If you look at the banners in the background
you'll see the name of the school: Harbor

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:36.470
High.

00:10:36.470 --> 00:10:39.500
This is the same area that Look-See ends up
prowling throughout Season 1, which takes

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.300
place a 80-90 years later.

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:45.150
The spread out farm houses in the middle of
nowhere eventually become a community.

00:10:45.150 --> 00:10:49.610
A high school is built, but Look-See remains
the area all the while to make sure it's citizens

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:51.769
always release their sorrows.

00:10:51.769 --> 00:10:55.930
Remember how I said Leah looks a lot like
the guy's daughter in Season 1 Episode 3?

00:10:55.930 --> 00:11:00.600
They aren't the same person, or the same actress,
but I would theorize that girl and her father

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:02.790
are descendants of Leah Capshaw.

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:06.800
So the big question becomes: what happens
to the second Look-See with the blue gloves?

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:11.459
Well, you better subscribe to CryptTV to find
out in the next season of Look-See.

00:11:11.459 --> 00:11:16.540
And of course you'll be treated to more scary
short films every Tuesday, Thursday and Friday.

